        Strategy: try strict json.loads first (fast path, zero risk for already
        valid JSON), then retry once after the string-aware pre-clean. If both
        fail, raise Json5LiteError with an actionable message.
    
        `source` (optional) names the origin (e.g. a file path) so the error
        message points the user at the right place instead of a bare decode stack.
        """
